        <a:p><a:r><a:t>Wins/tracked by practice: Ops Excellence 7/14, Strategy 8/16, HR 5/14, Finance 7/20, T&amp;D 2/8. Pattern in losses: McKinsey entry above the sponsor (board/CEO relationship) before formal scoping — 3rd such loss in 18 months. Deloitte won on sector accelerators despite weaker proposal. Recent MCG wins: senior-in-the-work staffing, faster mobilization, technology-agnostic positioning.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>── Supporting claims ──</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>• "Brand preference (12) and relationship gap (10) account for 51% of losses; top competitors McKinsey (8), PwC (6), BCG (6)"</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>  — ./Data/pipeline/win_loss_analysis.csv</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>• "McKinsey took a $1.2M deal via board/CEO relationship before formal scoping — 3rd above-the-sponsor loss in 18 months; Deloitte won $900K energy RFP on sector accelerators; MCG ~$295/hr vs. boutiques $220–280, MBB $580–750"</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>  — ./Data/pipeline/competitive_intel.txt</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>── Data sources ──</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>• win_rate_by_practice (bar_chart): ./Data/pipeline/win_loss_analysis.csv</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody>
